# .TELNET opens a telnet link to the harness echo server through the ESP.
# tools/telnet-probe.lua types keys, opens and closes the EDIT menu, sends
# a block of data, and leaves with EDIT, then Q; run.sh checks the bytes the server got (see test/README.md).
# It runs at real speed, as all Next network software must.
server echo 7777
put @DOTS@/TELNET.DOT /dot/TELNET
autostart ON ERROR ERROR TO e,l:POKE 23692,255:PRINT "ERR ";e;" ";l:FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0:NEXT i
autostart .TELNET 127.0.0.1 7777
autostart POKE 23692,255:PRINT "AFTER"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0:NEXT i
seconds 40
noreset 7.5
screen 39 Connection closed
screen 39 AFTER
